// SA-facing contracts for base64 codecs (sa_std built-in, 2026-10-26).
// All three symbols were already implemented and declared in
// sa_std.h; only the .sai declarations were missing.
// Two decode shapes exist and are NOT interchangeable:
// - sa_b64dec_simd: raw bulk fast path into a caller buffer. Standard
//   alphabet; stops at the first non-alphabet char (including '='),
//   so it does NOT consume padding. The caller provides at least
//   data_len/4*3 bytes of out and gets back the bytes written. Use
//   for clean unpadded streams only.
// - sa_deno_atob: full std.base64 decode (padding-aware) into an
//   owned buffer handle; returns 0 on invalid input. Read the handle
//   via sa_fmt_buffer_data/len and free it with sa_fmt_buffer_free.
//   This is the faithful decode for data-URL payloads.
// Encoding exists only in the handle shape: sa_deno_btoa writes the
// standard padded encoding into an owned buffer handle (same
// read/free path as atob).
// NOTE: the product-invented name sa_base64_decode(ptr, len, out,
// cap) does not exist in sa_std; rebind call sites to sa_deno_atob.
@extern sa_b64dec_simd(&data: ptr, data_len: u64, &out: ptr) -> u64
@extern sa_deno_btoa(&data: ptr, data_len: u64) -> u64
@extern sa_deno_atob(&data: ptr, data_len: u64) -> u64

// base64url (RFC 4648 section 5) in caller-buffer form, added with
// the STD batch-4 crypto suite (implemented in
// src/runtime/sa_crypto.zig): the wire form is UNPADDED (the JWT /
// JWK spelling); the decoder also tolerates trailing '=' padding.
// Status model matches crypto.sai: 0 ok, out_len is set to the
// needed size first, 9 (truncated) when cap is too small, 1
// (invalid) on non-alphabet input.
@extern sa_base64url_encode(&data: ptr, data_len: u64, &out: ptr, cap: u64, &out_len: ptr) -> i32
@extern sa_base64url_decode(&data: ptr, data_len: u64, &out: ptr, cap: u64, &out_len: ptr) -> i32
